        heading: "The Metro Codes structural review path",
        body: "Nashville's ePermits portal is the single intake for structural review across the consolidated government: application, sealed drawing upload, fee payment, reviewer assignment, correction cycles, and approval all live in one tracked system. Metro Codes' structural reviewers work from the adopted building code and expect the calculation package to reference the correct edition explicitly. Their comments tend to be specific and technical — a missing collector detail, a foundation detail that doesn't match the geotech report, a diaphragm nailing schedule that doesn't support the stated shear. We write our submittals for that level of reader: every calculation indexed to its drawing sheet, every assumption stated, every delegated-design item designated as a deferred submittal with criteria. Precision in, precision out.",
